<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Combinations in Real Life 3 - Village committee and farmer training</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) A village water committee is to be formed by selecting \({@pm@}\) men from \({@pa@}\) volunteers and \({@pw@}\) women from \({@pb@}\) volunteers. How many different committees are possible?</p>
<p>Number of committees = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>(b) A dairy farmers' cooperative has \({@pn2@}\) members. Four members will be chosen to attend a training on improved dairy farming. How many different groups of 4 members can be chosen?</p>
<p>Number of groups = [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Choose the men and the women separately, then multiply because both selections happen together.</p>
<p>Men: \(_{ {@pa@} }C_{ {@pm@} } = {@pMen@}\). Women: \(_{ {@pb@} }C_{ {@pw@} } = {@pWomen@}\).</p>
<p>\(\text{Committees} = {@pMen@} \times {@pWomen@} = {@ta1@}\)</p>
<p>For part (b), the order in which members are chosen does not matter, so this is \(_{ {@pn2@} }C_4\):</p>
<p>\(_{ {@pn2@} }C_4 = \dfrac{ {@pn2@}!}{4!\,{@pn2-4@}!} = {@ta2@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
